# Architecture

## Core

- **Do not invent** missing classes, methods, or package APIs. Search the repo first; if unclear, **ask**.
- Prefer extending existing systems over parallel new frameworks.
- Damage pipeline: **NetworkDamageUtil** is the single entry point — do not bypass
- Docs SSOT: `NetworkDesign.md`, `CheerAndTutorialDesign.md`, `GameArchitectureBoundaries.md`
- Do **not** auto-promote Docs into new Rules/Skills without user approval

## Boundaries (respect)

- **Player:** input, movement, stamina, dodge, own lifecycle events — **no** Vosk / mic / cheer-submit logic
- **Enemy:** detect/chase/attack — local combat state
- **Stage systems:** win/fail, flow, save I/O — keep responsibilities split (no UI owning gameplay state)
- **UI:** display/subscribe only (e.g. Cheer HUD listens to replicated buff/state) — **no** mic ownership or Vosk
- **Camera:** follow/view only (`ThirdPersonCamera`)
- **Cheer/Voice:** independent subsystem  
  - Detect: **Owner** `CheerKeywordEngine` (Vosk on **worker thread**; match/submit on **main**)  
  - Submit: `SubmitCheerServerRpc` → **Host** `CheerService` apply buff  
  - Mic: Dissonance owns capture in multi; **no double** `Microphone.Start`  
  - Do not stuff Cheer/Vosk into `Player` / random UI; extend `CheerKeywordEngine` / `CheerService` (ask before new entry points)

## Online-only (permanent lock)

- **Offline / solo-offline mode does not exist.** Solo 1-player uses `OnlineHost` (NGO). Any code, comment, or branch that references "offline", "isOnline == false", or "solo offline" must be **deleted**, not kept dormant.
- `LobbyContext.IsOnline` is always `true` — keep as constant, remove dead branches.
- Every gameplay feature is designed for 1–4 player **online** sessions. No parallel offline path.

## Scope lock (permanent)

- Work targets **full release**, not just demo. Do not scope-limit fixes or features to demo-only.
- Demo and release share the same codebase — no demo-fork logic.

## Don't

- Don't add reconnect / late-join / host-migration designs (unsupported)
- Don't create duplicate damage pipelines alongside `NetworkDamageUtil`
- Don't run Vosk `AcceptWaveform` on the main thread
- Don't add offline fallback branches — NGO is always running (solo = Host 1-player)
